    "q-39335": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39335",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "If $u=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ are orthogonal vectors, then $k=$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot 1+4\\cdot k+(-5)\\cdot 5+(-3)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =-5+4k-25-18 \\\\  & =4k-48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the dot product to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4k-48 & =0 \\\\ 4k & =48 \\\\ k & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
