    "q-39894": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39894",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ k \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ k \\\\ -1 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that $a⊥b.$ Find the value of $k.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $a$ and $b$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1}+{a}_{2}\\cdot {b}_{2}+{a}_{3}\\cdot {b}_{3}+{a}_{4}\\cdot {b}_{4} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot (-2)+k\\cdot k+2\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot k \\\\  & =6+{k}^{2}-2-4k \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-4k+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the dot product to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}-4k+4 & =0 \\\\ (k-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ k & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
